{{Quote|Narkina 5."<br />"What? What's that, what's Narkina 5?|A Niamos [[Coastal defender stormtrooper|shoretrooper]] dispatches Cassian Andor to the prison barge headed to the Narkina 5 Prison Complex|<ref name="Narkina 5" />}}
'''Narkina 5''', also known as '''Narkina''', was a small [[water]] [[moon]] that [[orbit]]ed the [[gas giant]] [[Narkina]]. The [[Galactic Empire]] maintained a [[Narkina 5 Imperial Prison Complex|prison complex]] there.

==Description==
Narkina 5,<ref name="DOF" /> also known as Narkina,<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]''</ref> was a small [[moon]] that orbited a [[gas giant]]. It was mostly covered by [[water]] but also had rocky islands, inlets, [[mesa]]s, [[lake]]s, and [[beach]]es with massive canyons and dry [[tree]]s.<ref name="Narkina 5 Audio" /> The lakes and rivers of the planet were rich with [[squigglies]] which [[fisher]]men from many [[species]], including [[Keredian]]s, visited the moon to [[Fishing|fish]], but<ref name="DOF" /> by [[5 BBY]]<ref name="AndorS1Date">{{AndorDate|1}}</ref> the Prison Complex had irreparably polluted the waters, diminishing the squigglie population and angering the fishermen communities.<ref name="DOF" />

==History==
In 5 BBY,<ref name="AndorS1Date" /> [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] was sent to the moon's [[Narkina 5 Imperial Prison Complex|Imperial Prison Complex]] after being arrested and [[Prisoner|sentenced]] on [[Niamos]]. The hundreds of prisoners there were forced to work twelve hour shifts to build [[EP-N5 fastener]]s for the Empire.<ref name="Narkina 5" /> Later, Andor and fellow prisoner [[Ruescott Melshi]] fled across the moon's surface after the [[Narkina 5 prison escape]].<ref name="One Way Out">{{Andor|One Way Out}}</ref>

{{Moon-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Narkina 5 was first pictured in the teaser trailer for the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' television series released on [[May 26]], [[2022]].<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|j5UX1Adanis|Andor &#124; Teaser Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/andor-teaser-trailer}}</ref> It first appeared in "[[Narkina 5 (episode)|Narkina 5]]," the eighth episode of the series,<ref name="Narkina 5" /> which aired on [[October 26]], 2022.<ref name="Airdate">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1557442379975573504|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-08-10|quote=This is what revolution looks like. Watch #Andor, a Star Wars Original Series, streaming only on @DisneyPlus September 21.|archivedate=20220810191942}}</ref> The scene on the moon's beach was photographed in Middle Peak Quarry in [[Wikipedia:Wirksworth|Wirksworth]], [[Wikipedia:Derbyshire|Derbyshire]] in the [[Wikipedia:United Kingdom|United Kingdom]].<ref name="Guide">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e11-trivia-gallery|text="Daughter of Ferrix" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref> When discussing the prison, in an [[Wikipedia:Entertainment Weekly|''Entertainment Weekly'']] interview published the same days as the StarWars.com article, the series' creator and executive producer, [[Tony Gilroy]], described Meero's all-female prison as hypothetically being Narkina 2 or Narkina 7 as opposed to Narkina 5.<ref name="EW">{{WebCite|url=https://ew.com/andor-creator-tony-gilroy-explains-surprise-ending-final-shot-11731474|text=''Andor'' creator Tony Gilroy explains that surprise ending and final shot|author=Ross, Dalton|date=2025-05-14|archivedate=20250516141415}}</ref> Gilroy had also previously mentioned Narkina 2 as a hypothetical location for the Empire's [[alien]] prisoners when discussing Narkina 5 in an interview with [[Wikipedia:Valnet#Collider|''Collider'']] on [[November 22]], [[2022]].<ref name="Collider">{{WebCite|url=https://collider.com/andor-aliens-explained-tony-gilroy-comments|text=Why 'Andor' Doesn't Have Many 'Star Wars' Aliens Explained By Showrunner Tony Gilroy [Exclusive&#93;|author=Lovitt, Maggie|date=2022-11-22|work=[[Wikipedia:Valnet#Collider|''Collider'']]|archivedate=20250315010102}}</ref>

